messages:   15%|#4        | 73/500 [04:45<17:52,  2.51s/it][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 703 and 973?', '\n\nTo find the product of **703** and **973**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nStart by expressing each number as a sum of smaller parts to make multiplication easier.\n\n\\[\n703 = 700 + 3\n\\]\n\\[\n973 = 900 + 73\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nMultiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n703 \\times 973 = (700 + 3) \\times (900 + 73)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 700 \\times 900 + 700 \\times 73 + 3 \\times 900 + 3 \\times 73\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **First Part:**\n\\[\n700 \\times 900 = 630,\\!000\n\\]\n\n2. **Second Part:**\n\\[\n700 \\times 73 = 51,\\!100\n\\]\n\n3. **Third Part:**\n\\[\n3 \\times 900 = 2,\\!700\n\\]\n\n4. **Fourth Part:**\n\\[\n3 \\times 73 = 219\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Parts Together\n\n\\[\n630,\\!000 + 51,\\!100 + 2,\\!700 + 219 = 683,\\!019\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{683,\\!019}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is ']]
