final_output:  ['87,420.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **310** and **282**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   310 \\times 282 = 310 \\times (200 + 80 + 2)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 310 by each part separately:**\n\n   - **Multiply by 200:**\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 200 = 62,\\!000\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 80:**\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 80 = 24,\\!800\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 2:**\n     \\[\n     310 \\times 2 = 620\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add all the results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   62,\\!000 + 24,\\!800 + 620 = 87,\\!420\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{87,\\!420}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of **310** and **282** is **87,420**.', '']
