messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 684 and 663?', "\n\nTo find the product of **684** and **663**, we'll perform the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nLet's express both numbers in terms of their place values:\n\n\\[\n684 = 600 + 80 + 4\n\\]\n\\[\n663 = 600 + 60 + 3\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part\nWe'll use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n684 \\times 663 &= (600 + 80 + 4) \\times (600 + 60 + 3) \\\\\n&= 600 \\times 600 + 600 \\times 60 + 600 \\times 3 \\\\\n&\\quad + 80 \\times 600 + 80 \\times 60 + 80 \\times 3 \\\\\n&\\quad + 4 \\times 600 + 4 \\times 60 + 4 \\times 3\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Multiplication\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n600 \\times 600 &= 360,\\!000 \\\\\n600 \\times 60 &= 36,\\!000 \\\\\n600 \\times 3 &= 1,\\!800 \\\\\n80 \\times 600 &= 48,\\!000 \\\\\n80 \\times 60 &= 4,\\!800 \\\\\n80 \\times 3 &= 240 \\\\\n4 \\times 600 &= 2,\\!400 \\\\\n4 \\times 60 &= 240 \\\\\n4 \\times 3 &= 12 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n360,\\!000 &+ 36,\\!000 + 1,\\!800 \\\\\n&+ 48,\\!000 + 4,\\!800 + 240 \\\\\n&+ 2,\\!400 + 240 + 12 \\\\\n&= 360,\\!000 + 36,\\!000 = 396,\\!000 \\\\\n396,\\!000 + 1,\\!800 &= 397,\\!800 \\\\\n397,\\!800 + 48,\\!000 &= 445,\\!800 \\\\\n445,\\!800 + 4,\\!800 &= 450,\\!600 \\\\\n450,\\!600 + 240 &= 450,\\!840 \\\\\n450,\\!840 + 2,\\!400 &= 453,\\!240 \\\\\n453,\\!240 + 240 &= 453,\\!480 \\\\\n453,\\!480 + 12 &= 453,\\!492 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{453,\\!492}\n\\]. Therefore, the answer is "]]
