final_output:  ["628,680.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **930** and **676**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nFirst, let's break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts using the distributive property.\n\n\\[\n930 \\times 676 = 930 \\times (600 + 70 + 6)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Part Separately\n\n1. **Multiply 930 by 600:**\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 600 = 558,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 930 by 70:**\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 70 = 65,\\!100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 930 by 6:**\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 6 = 5,\\!580\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Add All the Products Together\n\nNow, add the results of the three multiplications:\n\n\\[\n558,\\!000 + 65,\\!100 + 5,\\!580 = 628,\\!680\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{628,\\!680}\n\\]", '']
