final_output:  ['195,300 + 11,718 = 207,018.\n\\].\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **651** and **318**, follow these easy-to-understand steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Multiplication\nUse the distributive property to simplify the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n651 \\times 318 = 651 \\times (300 + 18)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply by 300\n\\[\n651 \\times 300 = 651 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 1,\\!953 \\times 100 = 195,\\!300\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Multiply by 18\nFirst, break down 18 into 10 and 8:\n\n\\[\n651 \\times 18 = 651 \\times (10 + 8) = (651 \\times 10) + (651 \\times 8)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part:\n\n\\[\n651 \\times 10 = 6,\\!510\n\\]\n\\[\n651 \\times 8 = 5,\\!208\n\\]\n\nNow, add them together:\n\n\\[\n6,\\!510 + 5,\\!208 = 11,\\!718\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Add the Two Results\n\\[\n\\text{Therefore, the answer is } 195,\\!300 + 11,\\!718 = 207,\\!018\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{207,\\!018}\n\\]', '']
